#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "503204c2-5202-5eb6-9c99-1d89a4256bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300382}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300382} :answer-field/id #uuid "775ffea0-6f09-507b-ba4a-f5929a9c5ece" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301596} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d2ae08-199c-5474-adf2-cfd379ea5346" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300115}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300115} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fdb03f8-a8af-5dff-897a-1a48b028739f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8236cfbf-50c1-52a1-9051-6e2573a692b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300611}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300611} :answer-field/id #uuid "be04d349-7486-598b-9dcd-fc83d123cadf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cefa32c2-7378-5ecb-a3a0-9b87e829889e" :question/math-academy-id "q-326255" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right),\\,y=sin\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right),\\,0\\le t\\le 5.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | {{field-1}} | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi (2)}{4}\\right)=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=sin\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(3)=sin\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi (3)}{6}\\right)=sin\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=sin\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(1)=sin\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi (4)}{6}\\right)=sin\\,\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cda53e7-8da8-5d86-a98c-5728719bc41b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300000}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300000} :answer-field/id #uuid "926f273e-d8b0-5e4d-9631-40e611c24ed3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f796a4-f9bc-52c2-95c4-861c28462e0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300143}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300143} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c15bfd-ddd4-56df-9248-59fef4cfb8ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011fae4e-c40e-5543-bf07-c0c1656584a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299934}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299934} :answer-field/id #uuid "da7a0f49-5d74-598d-9cc7-a44f9d26dfa4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9040c3c-4511-5ef7-a719-36ef3ae85af2" :question/math-academy-id "q-326256" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right),\\,y=tan\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}\\right),\\,-1\\le t\\le 4.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(0),$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(0)=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi (0)}{2}\\right)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=tan\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(1)=tan\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi (1)}{3}\\right)=tan\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\right)=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi (2)}{2}\\right)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5261222-5c84-53d7-83dc-4815f45597be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300863}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300863} :answer-field/id #uuid "017f20f8-f3be-5028-8a3f-9c0169ff1daf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eec746e-403a-5509-a259-b2a25c7f614e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300105}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300105} :answer-field/id #uuid "08bf2134-aeb2-5dc1-89fe-6267bdf0284c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49dda00b-4cd7-585e-b882-2ec765cb77ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300338}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300338} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8cf1062-9505-5905-a983-1cd976df11d8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301831} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6c2c622-589c-57e8-8e2b-f4a0e13ed191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300956}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300956} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba198b2a-625a-56f7-832e-5a614a281fa8" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7a41944b-5b17-58c0-b340-9129937f3ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-326259" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2t-7,\\,y=3-t,\\,t\\le 4.\n$$\n\nDetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $x=2t-7\\le 1$ for all $t\\le 4.$ Consequently, the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 1.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that $y=3-t\\ge -1$ for all $t\\le 4.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302278 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030a64cf-fc76-5914-85f8-c09965785117" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299945}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299945} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fdfe631-b001-5c4d-9acb-599647a7f69e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301375} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aec764c0-a442-501c-b10b-4d44377629a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300835}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300835} :answer-field/id #uuid "6871eb3d-470a-5712-b672-933b7294159b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e0f124c2-4201-5bb3-865c-19b9f7b07595" :question/math-academy-id "q-326271" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2{t}^{2}-4t,\\,y=t+1,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nDetermine the range of $x.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{t}^{2}-4t \\\\  & =2({t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =2({t}^{2}-2t+1)-2 \\\\  & =2(t-1)^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2(t-1)^{2}\\ge 0,$ we can conclude that\n\n$$\nx\\ge -2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e94d1911-ed3d-5815-993c-5706bb6db9eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301118}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301118} :answer-field/id #uuid "2110a93e-f01d-5323-942b-6b3501be95e8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4edbddb5-72c7-5c76-b674-5d22d3545657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300374}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300374} :answer-field/id #uuid "8106cc74-d2b0-55db-a9b1-99ab5656e37f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4745021a-be38-5a65-8aeb-883e5154897a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300322}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300322} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b6368b0-9950-59b9-8c1c-4bd9dd90aab0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc13e0bc-45c8-5f01-a0e8-ab7650d6b391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300981}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300981} :answer-field/id #uuid "cda637cb-9571-5f86-bd7b-92db0577772d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d0d4a70a-5321-5bde-a4db-76e8b0c1223a" :question/math-academy-id "q-326300" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3-\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y=\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2}-1,\\,t\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nDetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $3-\\frac{1}{2}t\\le 2$ for all $t\\ge 2.$ Consequently, the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 2.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that $\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{2}-1\\ge 2$ for all $t\\ge 2.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302286 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcfaa7b5-c563-53e7-bd92-e6c6e8395aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300907}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300907} :answer-field/id #uuid "187d5fc8-6d6a-5f32-8688-bb8f0cd30671" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301306} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2815a46-b4d5-5f8d-bc82-d6e5d36ea87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300779}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300779} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eff2705-c8d2-58e1-8bc2-412880c9d806" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301435} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec1b6db-dcf7-5183-9f05-7a81452eee53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300520}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300520} :answer-field/id #uuid "49dffb7a-d9b2-570d-a601-f27888619af8" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301476} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217244d5-85da-5c1f-9377-eeaa16debb00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300124}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300124} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8515511-0d07-53a2-bb49-746ea67dfa91" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4a473799-9dcd-5e6d-9f92-4a1b0e38bad7" :question/math-academy-id "q-326304" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4t-{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2}+3,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-({t}^{2}-4t) \\\\  & =-({t}^{2}-4t+4)+4 \\\\  & =-(t-2)^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-(t-2)^{2}+4\\le 4,$ we conclude that the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 4.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that ${t}^{2}+3\\ge 3.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183eace4-e338-5bc7-9a8b-c34f12c92bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300063} :answer-field/id #uuid "1468603f-a543-5515-a97a-0150fa375a7b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301293} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da881d5a-28d4-5e93-a51d-56a0fa28f022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301045}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186301045} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b42eb7e-827b-599d-a098-30f18c64bcbe" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301417} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2580204-e34e-5d8c-a226-55c9acd1a4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300777}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300777} :answer-field/id #uuid "47fd0d80-4d34-54dd-8135-ca9d99535331" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/re