aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3} & \\text{ }{\\color{red}\\ge }-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\text{ }{\\color{red}\\ge }-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{3} & \\le -\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{4}{3} & \\le \\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le \\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le \\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-1\\le x\\le \\frac{5}{3}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{7}{3} & \\le \\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{7}{3}\\le \\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{29}{6} & \\le y\\le \\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{29}{6}\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054e45cb-ef1a-592f-8ce5-2215be471cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333032} {:answer/id #uuid "79eda04b-781c-5fda-aa4a-bb2479352bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334085} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6d0cbe-1f59-57f6-aefd-5d53e15a7b1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334353} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b9a71e-ffbd-5091-8899-773c38323464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334599} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb2865c-3deb-55d1-a152-eed996480e2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334599} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd68d1f-2e2e-53b3-8c88-e40a6b095d8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e9a5f727-046e-5c6d-b3a8-b57aa0e0de57" :question/math-academy-id "q-6742" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=t+1,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-6,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | ${\\color{blue}c}$ |\n| $y$ | ${\\color{blue}a}$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | ${\\color{blue}b}$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=(-3)^{2}-6=9-6=3.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb={0}^{2}-6=0-6=-6.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=3+1=4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b-c=3-(-6)-4=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335959 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ea7064-8984-5ac6-91ea-ed8921bbc138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333056} {:answer/id #uuid "827b89fe-a572-54cd-b9cb-dcc0569b217e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334153} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f91035-840a-59fe-a14a-8ded740896f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334736} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a7c0bf-869c-5788-8888-00b2ca3dcdac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334846} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2e747f-c905-58fc-9adb-fb9c26ba7608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334153} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a546347-737e-5d85-bf73-af24c4b5c1f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f35c183e-5200-5f54-ad21-69984c940bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-6825" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=3t-2,\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1},\\,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | ${\\color{blue}a}$ | $-8$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | ${\\color{blue}c}$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | ${\\color{blue}b}$ | $5$ | $10$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=3(-3)-2=-9-2=-11.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into $y=\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=\\frac{10}{(-2)^{2}+1}=\\frac{10}{5}=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=3(3)-2=9-2=7.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-11+2+7=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06475ed3-8f81-5f2a-92d7-37b61ba3d841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333047} {:answer/id #uuid "1675a734-ba42-53ad-bacc-d3d9a7ecfb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333190} {:answer/id #uuid "379b5cc9-a398-5f20-b13a-5820843260de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333501} {:answer/id #uuid "4e027385-3e35-564e-88cf-8f5955ad0320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333708} {:answer/id #uuid "bbabf68e-a37c-54df-b8af-32120f8b5dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334625}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333047} :answer-field/id #uuid "be306b92-cfe4-5ecc-9451-b14d1a1a3e42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cc1d2bf2-3dfe-5506-8434-072c2dc13cdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-69922" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=2t+1,\\,\\,\\,y=2t-1,\\,0\\le t\\le 5,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | ${\\color{blue}b}$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\n| $y$ | ${\\color{blue}a}$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | ${\\color{blue}c}$ | $9$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=2(0)-1=0-1=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=2t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=2(2)+1=4+1=5.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=2(4)-1=8-1=7.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b-c=-1-5-7=-13.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05970e26-5821-56d5-9192-cd54ac992296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1\\le x\\le 5,\\,-9\\le y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336077} {:answer/id #uuid "66a3960b-62dc-53fd-84aa-3678e0fb86aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 13,\\,3\\le y\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336947} {:answer/id #uuid "712b9c6e-788b-5ba0-8229-df8fca209a1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\le x\\le 6,\\,-13\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337040} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5bbdd7-51a4-577f-a287-db618f622b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 5,\\,-7\\le y\\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337327} {:answer/id #uuid "fa563dbb-82b3-57bc-8de5-0041f39c1575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6\\le x\\le 0,\\,1\\le y\\le 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338226}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337040} :answer-field/id #uuid "f957fa19-2286-54e9-bed6-f7be3613a470" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1fb3f2b5-56e5-553e-8562-5d6280836898" :question/math-academy-id "q-70523" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5,\\,\\,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -7,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+5 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5\\le 1+5 \\\\ 4 & \\le x\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $4\\le x\\le 6.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -6 & \\le 6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 6 \\\\ -6-7 & \\le 6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -7\\le 6-7 \\\\ -13 & \\le y\\le -1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-13\\le y\\le -1.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $4\\le x\\le 6$ and $-13\\le y\\le -1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "335d0d1c-7aa5-5e41-83dd-2bd696206902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339584} {:answer/id #uuid "45b4e8f6-0254-586e-8b2c-8ca34c9155e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 1,\\,y\\le 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339747} {:answer/id #uuid "760a81e8-5ce1-5b78-9884-f109dafe3e65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -1,\\,y\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340179} {:answer/id #uuid "94d1ef80-cf3c-5620-bee7-53c5c5629fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 1,\\,y\\le 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340466} {:answer/id #uuid "e778c967-2eb3-5de6-8c75-2e13c5bc4346" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -1,\\,y\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341172}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339584} :answer-field/id #uuid "043f62a1-3349-567c-aec9-24574a79034c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8f5b7d05-a282-5021-9aa5-8966b1c2524c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73623" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{t-2}+1,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{3}+2,\\,t\\ge 2,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $\\sqrt{t-2}\\ge 0$ for all $t\\ge 2.$ Consequently, $x=\\sqrt{t-2}+1\\ge 1.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that ${t}^{3}\\ge 8$ for all $t\\ge 2.$ Consequently, $y={t}^{3}+2\\ge 8+2=10.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x\\ge 1$ and $y\\ge 10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342038 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f6b6688-7ebd-5b25-83b7-5c07ad7c688a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\le x\\le 5,\\,1\\le y\\le 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339270} {:answer/id #uuid "25d8d7af-c8e4-5ebb-980e-a55d3a4cd6d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 3,\\,-5\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339454} {:answer/id #uuid "3320f739-78f0-51e9-9081-4e93b3163fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1\\le x\\le 4,\\,-1\\le y\\le 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339582} {:answer/id #uuid "94fae60d-72de-52be-8e5a-de4200f76d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1\\le x\\le 6,\\,-5\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340469} {:answer/id #uuid "dbd74067-cc9b-5848-b108-229097ff8d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,-5\\le y\\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341079}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339454} :answer-field/id #uuid "b483317f-a4a2-5639-8bcf-ae196dafce5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341697}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f2f3822c-027f-5b78-99af-6944b4b3bf81" :question/math-academy-id "q-73626" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 2 & \\text{ }{\\color{red}\\ge }-2\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\text{ }{\\color{red}\\ge }-2 \\\\ -2 & \\le -2\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 2 \\\\ 1-2 & \\le 1-2\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1+2 \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-1\\le x\\le 3.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -2 & \\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 2 \\\\ -2-3 & \\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3\\le 2-3 \\\\ -5 & \\le y\\le -1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-5\\le y\\le -1.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $-1\\le x\\le 3$ and $-5\\le y\\le -1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fcf5022-4812-5cf2-a745-37302fcd5dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le -1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339275} {:answer/id #uuid "4915a118-a0a0-5db9-914a-1721d3b42565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\le x\\le 1,\\,-2\\le y\\le 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339784} {:answer/id #uuid "b457cadc-b9f6-5c2c-9f2c-42f3a633bbd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340764} {:answer/id #uuid "d4206d0e-3e82-51c1-8e8c-9cad7033e6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1\\le x\\le 3,\\,-1\\le y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341005} {:answer/id #uuid "e66ef8b5-6026-532a-a34b-a4ed72b384c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341166}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340764} :answer-field/id #uuid "c59dee8b-2e72-5994-98ef-02b4aa2af213" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cbbe4cfc-6544-53d2-868c-0f7ad468266a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73632" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{3}{2},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -2 & \\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 2 \\\\ -2+1 & \\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1\\le 2+1 \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-1\\le x\\le 3.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2} & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\frac{3}{2}\\le \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1 & \\le y\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $1\\le y\\le 2.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $-1\\le x\\le 3$ and $1\\le y\\le 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387437 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3809196-0e72-568a-acb4-8f1806b011f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d1/d1cec5ea2da4a0b5f141bb24b4addc797defbc48e76cdfdbfab3a303e348b8cc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387439} {:answer/id #uuid "d44a46da-960a-5000-b573-28968c62249a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bc/bcb2b08bab14ce74347d37a0e896451750db0203ab830b835a83de6b7a81b61d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387440} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c8555e-f76d-58d2-98de-66b72a2089cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/02/02b248ea373f295fa4dbad215eba4c211ef18548dca4a56d57cb3f15424ad501.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387441} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbecde8-5a29-5731-8756-dcd4a93b4487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/09/097262c9e70a68d3a7ae1b1186bed57cefd7b99b0af2215d4ce6b08a086f90c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387442} {:answer/id #uuid "63870ff1-4a2f-5845-b126-b062e8aa81ef" :answe