t{3}$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/47/47615688bf550384de29a5e7e480bdab699b8eee994e5e28052e4d043e2db503.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c70aaa5a-5e55-5cac-9a6f-6318d6836204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d0/d06dfa9b8f6e87944014aa3eb03b6f83bd43e90624ba84d5d93d1d7f4e3beea6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393322} {:answer/id #uuid "ac220e89-32ea-508e-929a-c803d138ccfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0e/0e7f02989d53152d1f2d5247f7f42d579956e49743694229d409cd266ec33e46.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393323} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee90a69-8fe7-5272-8b17-1772dc5a0e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/9c/9c8ed7ce4ee431e67b923ce3028819eb9f6f6b0a52cb892c93e582c31ba9d8af.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393324} {:answer/id #uuid "e95ca3e9-ccf0-585e-a54f-3195d2e34519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/89/89b88f56878aeb33afe775e083c3775aaa701b6d293ca62e0bd3f2a78923159a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393325} {:answer/id #uuid "1d979614-76c4-5da3-9edd-dc0cf04890c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/1a/1a7c98897aa0c13daff168b3804ac292c7662ee21f313ddd9e631019bcfbb814.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393326}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393323} :answer-field/id #uuid "8985fe72-57b1-51f4-bcff-4b1407775690" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b3e6469c-9ac4-59c2-95ba-5849e3955d1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73602" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=2t-1,\\,\\,\\,y=2-{t}^{2},\\,-3\\le t\\le 3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=2-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $-7$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/5c/5cd074670c05cea0c68db75c7e1a57309c017c97556e976f2db4c3bf1b358a85.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c848ce1a-65b8-563c-9fec-80599c592bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le -3,\\,y\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400116} {:answer/id #uuid "7f194208-efc2-515c-a071-37d890d6515f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 2,\\,y\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400117} {:answer/id #uuid "2b898a9d-7842-5e4a-9365-22c2934152ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\le 2,\\,y\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400118} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1c0d33-169a-5055-a64e-c6a8e8656c1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge -1,\\,y\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400119} {:answer/id #uuid "658dd7e1-62d5-534e-8c6f-6d03db279945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\ge 3,\\,y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400120}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400118} :answer-field/id #uuid "acb683db-68cc-56c9-829b-45a54bf4f29a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a3e9c6f6-566c-5162-9fe9-4d86fd16d1a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-123769" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3-t,\\,\\,\\,y=t+2,\\,t\\ge 1,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $3-t\\le 2$ for all $t\\ge 1.$ Consequently, $x=3-t\\le 2.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that $t+2\\ge 3$ for all $t\\ge 1.$ Consequently, $y=t+2\\ge 3.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x\\le 2$ and $y\\ge 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400121 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "befcfe4a-abd3-5984-a1a3-1a1bf2b0cd72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-3\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400123} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee13255-e4e9-52e6-b06e-d0aeddb3bb38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400124} {:answer/id #uuid "c3236814-4c23-5fc9-a82d-b9432370c830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-3\\le y\\le -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400125} {:answer/id #uuid "bcd316cc-7219-5b56-b38c-fa0c32ea3d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-2\\le y\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400126} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb2b3dc-0e10-5966-a703-a0088b75ec08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400127}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400127} :answer-field/id #uuid "806b0a66-23a8-530b-9fd2-35a679c8dd3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "42535d46-cb00-5afc-82ab-e62c0ea06521" :question/math-academy-id "q-123773" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 1 & \\text{ }{\\color{red}\\ge }-\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\text{ }{\\color{red}\\ge }-1 \\\\ -1 & \\le -\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 1-1 & \\le 1-\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1+1 \\\\ 0 & \\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -1+2 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\le 1+2 \\\\ 1 & \\le y\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $1\\le y\\le 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64998bfc-bfc7-5d3e-8ee6-300d3a38797d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-4\\le y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400130} {:answer/id #uuid "42492b12-0052-541d-8cee-a36023e92984" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-3\\le y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400131} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4ef62b-01d3-5f37-819a-bf2a72b19db1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,-3\\le y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400132} {:answer/id #uuid "79eb9da7-f01c-5dfb-a236-47a585231977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,2\\le y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400133} {:answer/id #uui