db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186526291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4077e1f2-8ed8-570d-a121-a371589a3612" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta -\\frac{5}{3},\\,y=-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta -\\frac{7}{4},\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}}{{field-2}}$x\\le ${{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-4}}$\\le y${{field-5}}{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta\\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & \\le -\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{3} & \\le -\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta -\\frac{5}{3}\\le \\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{25}{6} & \\le x\\le \\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{25}{6}\\le x\\le \\frac{5}{6}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}\\theta\\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & \\le -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{7}{4} & \\le -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta -\\frac{7}{4}\\le \\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{7}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{21}{4} & \\le y\\le \\frac{7}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{21}{4}\\le y\\le \\frac{7}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/