he ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is {{field-1}}{{field-2}}$x\\le ${{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is {{field-4}}$\\le y${{field-5}}{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta\\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4} & \\le -\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta \\le \\frac{5}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4}-\\frac{5}{2} & \\le -\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{cos}\\theta -\\frac{5}{2}\\le \\frac{5}{4}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{15}{4} & \\le x\\le -\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{15}{4}\\le x\\le -\\frac{5}{4}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}\\theta\\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2} & \\le -\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta \\le \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{1}{3} & \\le -\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\\theta +\\frac{1}{3}\\le \\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{25}{6} & \\le y\\le \\frac{29}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{25}{6}\\le y\\le \\frac{29}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535253 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080aabc3-c827-576c-9cd0-ad92ebca357a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6a/6a02899ff0058a5724bd786531e5656722b48b586d5bbc9dc7cccd88cead0930.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535225} {:answer/id #uuid "53b15d34-777b-5ec8-a9ac-2a6a2621c159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ae/ae3f9909fc55f92e6373c249a7b50bb90a92c